<title>SINGAPORE: Wong's Circuit debuts at high of US$1.14.</title>
<headline>Wong's Circuit debuts at high of US$1.14.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Printed circuit board maker Wong's Circuits Holdings Ltd made its debut on the Singapore stock exchange at a high of US$1.14 per share in the early minutes on Thursday against its initial public offer price of US$0.88 each.  </p>
<p>At 0105 GMT, the shares eased towards US$1.07 on a turnover of over five million shares.</p>
<p>The Hong Kong-based company had offered a total of 43 million shares in its initial public offer, of which 34.4 million were placed with institutional investors.</p>
<p>Wong's Circuits makes printed circuit boards for customers in various industries including computers, telecommunications and consumer electronics.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703083)</p>
</text>
